  "full_response": "def fibonacci(n):\n    if n <= 1:\n        return n\n\n    # Initialize a list to store Fibonacci numbers. The list starts with the two base cases (F(0) = 0, F(1) = 1)\n    fibonacci_numbers = [0 1]\n    \n    # Start calculating from F(2) onward, up to n\n    for i in range(2, n + 1):\n        # The next number is the sum of the two preceding ones\n        next_number = fibonacci_numbers[i - 1] + fibonacci_numbers[i - 2]\n        # Append the next number to the list\n        fibonacci_numbers.append(next_number)\n\n    # Return the nth Fibonacci number\n    return fibonacci_numbers[n]\n\n# Example usage:\nn = 10\nprint(f\"The {n}th Fibonacci number is: {fibonacci(n)}\")\n",
